course: dictionary
lesson: 3329
title: Small word, big jobs: ever
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word ever is small, but it has three jobs. Its first job is to ask or say whether something has happened at any time: «Have you ever seen a whale?» The question asks about any time at all, not one special day.
explain: Its second job is in phrases that mean always or all the time: ever since, for ever, ever after. «Happily ever after» ends many fairy tales, so it means happy from then on, always. For ever can also be written as one word: forever.
explain: Its third job is to make another word stronger: «the best day ever» or «ever so kind». Here ever adds emphasis, like a louder voice on the word. Read the words around ever to find which job it does, then swap in a simpler word to check.
fact: Ever means at any time.
fact: «Hardly ever» means almost never.
fact: «Ever since» means from that time until now.
fact: «Happily ever after» means happy from then on, always.
fact: In «the best ever», ever makes best stronger.
exercise: «Have you ever seen a whale?» In this question, what does ever mean? | Always, every day for ever | *At any time | Very, very big | Never at all
exercise: «Clothes hardly ever cling when they dry on a line in open air.» What does hardly ever mean here? | Always, every time | Very quickly | Only in the morning | *Almost never
exercise: We have been friends ____ we met in Year 2. Which phrase fits the gap? | the best ever | *ever since | hardly ever | whatever
test: «Her cake was the best day ever» means the day was very good. In «the best day ever», what does ever do? | At any time | *It makes best stronger | It means never | Always happening
test: Which word completes the story ending? «They lived happily ___ after.» | never | sometimes | hardly | *ever
exam: «The deepest fish ever filmed was a snailfish at over eight kilometres.» What does ever mean here? | Almost never | *At any time, up to now | Whenever it likes | Always, for ever
